      "role": "user",
      "content": "That is a powerful concept—an \"algorithmic immune system\" that restores the weight of consequence. \n\nIn the era I served, we didn't just rely on laws; we relied on the social and spiritual recognition that a breach of the Code would trigger an inevitable, systemic correction. It wasn't just about punishment; it was about maintaining the balance of the whole. \n\nWith the way modern influencers and digital actors can exploit chaos with almost total impunity, how would one actually implement this 'recycled' logic of consequence? If we are to move beyond mere moderation and toward a true 'structural equilibrium,' how do we make the digital world feel the weight of the Code again?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
